  "title": "Silent Night",
  "composer": "Franz Xaver Gruber",
  "about": "Franz Xaver Gruber wrote this tune for Christmas Eve 1818, in Oberndorf near Salzburg. The young priest Joseph Mohr had written the words, and Gruber set them to music. Mohr played the guitar at the first performance, and the song later travelled far beyond Austria.",
  "funFact": "In 2011, the Austrian Commission for UNESCO added Silent Night to Austria's list of intangible cultural heritage.",
